ManSection.Description:
    If the third argument chunksize is given, it specifies the
    length of the interval which is sieved in one go using the Sieve of
    Eratosthenes. Longer sieving intervals increase the memory requirements
    and the time needed for initially setting up the iterator, but make
    iterating over many prime powers faster.


gap> iter := PrimePowersIterator();
<iterator of prime powers>
gap> repeat q := NextIterator(iter); until PowerModInt(2,q-1,q^2)=1;
gap> q;
1093
gap> iter := PrimePowersIterator(1000000);;
gap> qs := [];;
gap> for q in iter do Add(qs,q); od; 
gap> Length(qs);
78734
gap> Number([1..1000000],IsPrimePowerInt);
78734
gap> iter := PrimePowersIterator(10000000,100000);;
gap> qs := [];;
gap> for q in iter do Add(qs,q); od;
gap> Length(qs);
665134
